    "result_text": "The full build passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`), with the acceptance test green and no other tests broken.\n\n## Summary\n\nI consolidated the three separate duplicate checks (telephone, email, household) into a single derived `identityKey` and made an exact whole-key match the only 409 condition.\n\n**The key** \u2014 `identityKey = normalizedTelephone + \"|\" + (email or empty) + \"|\" + householdId`, each segment canonicalized the way it's stored (E.164 phone, lower-cased email, shared household id; empty segments when absent).\n\n**New code** (in `rest/function/owner`):\n- `IdentityKeys` \u2014 the one place the key is derived. `of(Owner)` for stored owners; `of(OwnerFieldsDto, repo)` for the incoming request, which resolves the household id the owner *would* be assigned so a re-submitted household member still collides.\n- `EnsureUniqueIdentity` \u2014 the single check step: builds the request's key and rejects only when it equals an existing owner's whole key.\n- `DuplicateIdentityException` + `DuplicateIdentityExceptionHandler` + escalation YAML \u2192 409.\n- `Households.resolveHouseholdId(...)` \u2014 reuses the existing `matches`/`id` logic (mirrors `AssignHousehold`) so household resolution isn't duplicated.\n\n**Wiring changes:**\n- `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 replaced the `ensureUniqueTelephone \u2192 ensureUniqueEmail \u2192 ensureUniqueHousehold` chain with one `ensureUniqueIdentity` step, kept before `build`/`assignHousehold` so rejection happens before any mutation.\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added the read-only `identityKey` property to the `Owner` schema (so it's returned).\n- `OwnerMapper` \u2014 populates `identityKey` via `IdentityKeys.of(owner)` on every `OwnerDto`.\n\n**Removed:** the three `EnsureUnique*` steps, their three `Duplicate*Exception` classes, three handlers, and three escalation YAMLs.\n\n**Behaviour change, as specified:** because telephone is only one part of the key, two members of the same household with different telephones now have different keys and are both allowed \u2014 a same-telephone request is a duplicate only when its email and household id also match exactly. The acceptance test's collision case (same telephone, both no email, both non-shared \u2192 equal keys) correctly returns 409.",
